<description>&lt;p&gt;Ecuador is facing simultaneous security and humanitarian shocks as criminal networks expand in Quito and the military conducts its first land operation against cartels with US assistance, while heavy rains on Santa Cruz Island killed one person and left two missing. A priest was killed when a crucifix fell on him, prompting an archbishop to announce a safety plan for clergy. The government continues to detain opposition leader Luisa González on money-laundering charges. The crisis previously recorded two battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxOOVJvWUdRcVpIU2h0amJQQmJpZlQ5UFAtTEVKZy13b2l4RkJlSDEwNkhiZUFKWXlsMG56YmdUbk1tTFlOWEVlOU1ySHNFQUtNWUtLZzZyUGxlWmNzTmNuem9oVEg5MzVqWWRJSUMzSnBIZzczSmdqZ0RkSy1wR3dTaXZlS3Z4TUktenYyZ0N1VDFBc28?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC Wildlife Magazine&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxNRjFCLVBIa0JOcTVHcDdmcTVaRnRNMTJVcUFCMnRCOVdOOENZVTcyRGJpYVZjQnowRVpmdDh5SG1DUjl5OHR4SlQ1eVZjZ1QyblVZak0yRndCTzQ4eHg5eFl6eEZoUEZzWjYwQTROLVpzUlVZOU5kbGd4dVZwX0N2RDNXUk9UaWhEQWpVeC1EM3gxOUtYTHE4UGhRem5STk5LMWJHUWxHTHJHbzZxdGROWVdzemxWUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxQVXpwSW50SURCdXJJNlB4dnFJUEs2aG5pRThvb2dyalpmNF92UU1ocU5remJ5QVUxN2Y2N3IycHJEZHhLMmE1QTRWNGlwcURNSjNoSTNaZG1FdFBtSHZoUTUtaWxJT2Etckh1Y0hpbGdVWjEtUU56MVZGVFU2Qi1aVDBHR2toSGhabWFveXoycXlhY2NiSXpWTmpmbEhyamhKNVY0LU5XblJZTy1RWnJiS0plektMVGtxVkd5Rm9LMi0?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Monitor&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Inquirer.net&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxPdTFiQ1BEUGZJNHFrd2JHOW1HNXdxdlZZbFlobDJ3UEtuV0hJUGFubXZXaHVHZWdDbm1uVHQ4aERRdWVYRkoxY1dPdktpVEdOZ0k4c3hCWHhmSU95eWYtZS1XRi1rVmN0VDB